      "claim": "A lower-similarity analogue with a chloro instead of fluoro substituent and methylamino instead of cyclopropylamino showed poor Bu/Pu (0.11), but this is outweighed by the high-similarity GNE-7915 data.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Pass: the query is a close analogue of GNE-7915 (Morgan similarity 0.797), which shows consistent high CNS penetration across rat and NHP with unbound CSF/plasma and brain/plasma ratios of 0.6-0.83. The conservative cyclopropylamino-for-ethylamino change preserves the brain-penetrant pharmacophore, and lower-similarity poor-penetration analogues are less transferable.",
